I came across this sentence:
"Usually, but not always, a country coincides with a sovereign territory."
As I understand it, "mapti" is about two distinguishable things
fitting to one another. In the example, "a country" and "a sovereign
territory" are identical rather than being in the relation of
ontologically distinct correspondence.

